+## Known traps
+
+- Browser suites drive the toolbar mostly at desktop with real clicks
+  (`page.click('.filter-pill[data-filter="salves"]')` at 1200px in
+  `test-challenger2-adversarial.browser.test.js:138`;
+  `page.click('#filterRow button[data-filter="gift-sets"]')` at 1366px in
+  `gift-set-variants.browser.test.js:103`; `page.click("#openOrderStatusBtn")`
+  at 1200px in test-challenger2-adversarial 351/469). At 375px they use
+  `document.querySelector(...).click()` / `btn.click()` inside `evaluate`
+  (`extended_qa_test.js:469,501`, `puppeteer_tests.js:410` order-status)
+  which works on elements inside a closed `<dialog>` -- so keep the nodes
+  in the DOM, never `display:none` the individual pills, and never clone
+  them. `challenger-m2-verification.browser.test.js:375-382` counts
+  `.filter-pill` / `.concern-pill` at 375px (counts only).
+- `#resetFiltersBtn` is rendered by `renderCards()` in the empty grid and
+  handled by delegation on `grid`; `#shopCount` text is read by many suites
+  -- do not change its wording.
+- `syncShopUrl()` (main.js ~7261) writes ?category/?concern/?scent/?sort/?q
+  via replaceState; chip removal must go through the same state + `render()`
+  so the URL follows. Deep links (?category=, ?concern=, ?q=, #hash) are
+  applied in the block at ~7415; nothing there needs to change.
+- `scripts/a11y-check.js` INCOMPLETE_BASELINE pins `shop.html` at 105 per
+  theme; new always-visible-at-desktop nodes are none (the phone bar, chips
+  row and sheet are hidden/closed at the scan viewport), but if the number
+  moves, inspect the nodes before touching the pin.
+- `scripts/text-layout.browser.test.js` renders at 320/375/430 too: keep
+  the sticky row's buttons from clipping ("Filter" + badge + "Sort" next to
+  a `flex:1` search input at 320px).
+- `reveal-check.js` runs shop-adjacent pages at 375 with main.js delayed:
+  hiding `.shop-toolbar` via CSS on phones is fine (never painted), but do
